 "_doc": "Hebrew display names for derived concept families (docs/CONCEPTS.md §10). Key = the concept-id prefix shared by two or more concepts in the same category (config/concepts/*.json, src/catalog/concepts.js familyKey/resolveFamily) - a bare id with no hyphen counts as its own key, so 'zucchini' and 'zucchini-dark' share the key 'zucchini'. A prefix listed here with fewer than two concepts sharing it anywhere is an error (test/conceptFamilies.test.js) - remove the entry when the last sibling is removed or renamed, so this file cannot rot. A prefix with siblings but no entry here falls back to the shortest sibling's own name (src/catalog/concepts.js resolveFamily); most of the groups below exist so that fallback isn't the one users see. Not a concept file: excluded from conceptFiles()/index.json, loaded by name (FAMILIES_FILE). | groups (14.10, docs/CONCEPTS.md §17): the optional fourth level between a department and its families - { \"<groupId>\": { \"name\": \"<Hebrew>\", \"category\": \"<department>\", \"families\": [\"<familyId>\", ...] } }. A group lives in one department; a family is in at most one group; a family not listed anywhere sits directly under its department (group null). Navigation only - substitution never climbs to a group (Naor 14.10).",
